fixed: ["Pick criterion: the page now picks by one stated rule, the most measured usable energy that a kit's own panels can fill in one sunny day (6 full-sun hours or less at nameplate), among kits a US buyer can order today. Applied to every row in a new 'How the pick is made' section at the top of the after-section, using only the page's own figures. Elite 200 V2 + 2×200 W wins (1,910 Wh measured, 5.2 h). Both AC180 kits qualify but hold 1,030 Wh. Elite 200 V2 + 200 W ($0.63/usable Wh) needs 10.4 h. C1000 Gen 2 + 100 W needs 10.2 h. ALLPOWERS R2500 V2 has no measured figure, so it can't be ranked. Zendure (sold out), STREAM Ultra (Utah only, no panels) and Solarbank (no US listing) are out. No new facts were needed.", "Must phrase 2 changed from '1,910 Wh measured, $0.78 per usable Wh' to '1,910 Wh measured, filled in 5.2 h of full sun' to match the criterion. Must phrase 1 kept and appears verbatim in the answer. Row 1 refill cell now reads '5.2 h: fills in one sunny day'. Row 1 is still the pick.", "Answer rewritten to answer the question first, in its words. It names the Zendure SolarFlow kit (US: sold out), EcoFlow STREAM Ultra (Utah only), Anker SOLIX Solarbank (Europe only) and BLUETTI Balco (not on BLUETTI's US store), each with the US status already sourced on the page. It then gives the US pick. Text is about 298 characters by hand count, under the 300 limit. The 'Short answer.' label was dropped to fit, and I could not run a script to check the count.", "Added one after-
